{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n\n    >>> largest_divisor(15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    # Iterate from 2 up to the square root of n.\n    # If a divisor 'i' is found, n // i is the largest proper divisor.\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return n // i\n\n    # If no divisors are found in the loop, n must be prime, so its largest proper divisor is 1.\n    return 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of prime factors for a given integer `n`, sorted ascending with multiplicities. The product of factors equals `n`.\"\"\"\n    factors = []\n    d = 2\n    temp_n = n\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 1\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n    return factors"}
