{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Dict\n\n# Module-level dictionary for memoization.\n# This stores previously computed FibFib numbers to avoid redundant calculations.\n_memo: Dict[int, int] = {\n    0: 0,\n    1: 0,\n    2: 1\n}\n\ndef fibfib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th FibFib number using memoization for efficiency.\n    The sequence is defined by fibfib(0)=0, fibfib(1)=0, fibfib(2)=1, and fibfib(n) = fibfib(n-1) + fibfib(n-2) + fibfib(n-3) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Recursive case for n > 2\n    result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "```python\ndef vowels_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Counts vowels ('a','e','i','o','u') in a string, case-insensitive.\n    'y' is counted only if it's the last character of the word.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    lower_s = s.lower()\n    standard_vowels = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\n    for char in lower_s:\n        if char in standard_vowels:\n            count += 1\n\n    if lower_s.endswith('y'):\n        count += 1\n\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(x)\n    num_digits = len(s)\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        return s[::-1]\n    else:\n        effective_shift = shift % num_digits\n        return s[num_digits - effective_shift:] + s[:num_digits - effective_shift]\n```"}
