{"task_id": "HumanEval/84", "solution": "```python\ndef solve(N):\n    \"\"\"Given a positive integer N, return the total sum of its digits in binary.\n    Constraints: 0 \u2264 N \u2264 10000.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Calculate the sum of the decimal digits of N.\n    digit_sum = 0\n    for digit_char in str(N):\n        digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n\n    # Convert the calculated sum into its binary string representation.\n    if digit_sum == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    binary_digits = []\n    temp_sum = digit_sum\n    while temp_sum > 0:\n        binary_digits.append(str(temp_sum % 2))\n        temp_sum //= 2\n\n    return \"\".join(reversed(binary_digits))\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/84", "solution": "def solve(N):\n    \"\"\"Given a positive integer N, return the total sum of its digits in binary.\n\n    Example\n        For N = 1000, the sum of digits will be 1 the output should be \"1\".\n        For N = 150, the sum of digits will be 6 the output should be \"110\".\n        For N = 147, the sum of digits will be 12 the output should be \"1100\".\n\n    Variables:\n        @N integer\n             Constraints: 0 \u2264 N \u2264 10000.\n    Output:\n         a string of binary number\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (0 <= N <= 10000):\n        raise ValueError(\"N must be between 0 and 10000 inclusive.\")\n\n    sum_of_digits = sum(int(digit) for digit in str(N))\n\n    return bin(sum_of_digits)[2:]"}
