{"task_id": "HumanEval/83", "solution": "```python\ndef starts_one_ends(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return the count of the numbers of n-digit\n    positive integers that start or end with 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        # For n > 1:\n        # Count of n-digit numbers starting with 1: 1 * 10^(n-1)\n        # The first digit is 1, and the remaining (n-1) digits can be any of 0-9.\n        count_starts_with_1 = 10**(n - 1)\n\n        # Count of n-digit numbers ending with 1: 9 * 10^(n-2)\n        # The first digit can be any of 1-9 (cannot be 0), the last digit is 1,\n        # and the middle (n-2) digits can be any of 0-9.\n        count_ends_with_1 = 9 * (10**(n - 2))\n\n        # Count of n-digit numbers starting AND ending with 1: 1 * 10^(n-2)\n        # The first digit is 1, the last digit is 1, and the middle (n-2) digits can be any of 0-9.\n        count_starts_and_ends_with_1 = 10**(n - 2)\n\n        # Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion:\n        # Total = Count(starts with 1) + Count(ends with 1) - Count(starts AND ends with 1)\n        return count_starts_with_1 + count_ends_with_1 - count_starts_and_ends_with_1\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/81", "solution": "def numerical_letter_grade(grades: list[float]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Converts a list of numerical GPAs to a list of letter grades.\n    The conversion is based on a predefined grading scale.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # The grading scale, sorted in descending order of GPA threshold.\n    # This structure is derived from the design's GradeConverter and test cases.\n    GRADING_SCALE = [\n        (4.0, 'A+'),\n        (3.7, 'A'),\n        (3.3, 'A-'),\n        (3.0, 'B+'),\n        (2.7, 'B'),\n        (2.3, 'B-'),\n        (2.0, 'C+'),\n        (1.7, 'C'),\n        (1.3, 'C-'),\n        (1.0, 'D+'),\n        (0.7, 'D'),\n        (0.1, 'D-'),  # Correctly places D- for GPAs > 0.0 and < 0.7\n        (0.0, 'E')\n    ]\n\n    converted_grades = []\n    for gpa in grades:\n        letter_grade = 'E'  # Default to 'E' for values below the lowest explicit threshold (0.0).\n        for threshold, grade in GRADING_SCALE:\n            if gpa >= threshold:\n                letter_grade = grade\n                break  # Found the highest matching grade, assign and move to the next GPA.\n        converted_grades.append(letter_grade)\n\n    return converted_grades"}
