{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts characters within each word of a string based on ASCII value.\n    Preserves original word and space order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    tokens = re.split(r'(\\\\s+)', s)\n\n    processed_tokens = []\n    for token in tokens:\n        if token.strip() == '':\n            processed_tokens.append(token)\n        else:\n            processed_tokens.append(\"\".join(sorted(token)))\n\n    return \"\".join(processed_tokens)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting,\n    you will sort the given array in ascending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is odd,\n    or sort it in descending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    copied_array = list(array)\n\n    if not copied_array or len(copied_array) == 1:\n        return copied_array\n\n    # Determine sorting order based on the parity of the sum of first and last elements.\n    first_last_sum = copied_array[0] + copied_array[-1]\n\n    if first_last_sum % 2 != 0:  # Sum is odd, sort in ascending order.\n        copied_array.sort(reverse=False)\n    else:  # Sum is even, sort in descending order.\n        copied_array.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return copied_array\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting,\n    you will sort the given array in ascending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is odd,\n    or sort it in descending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is even.\n\n    Note:\n    * don't change the given array.\n\n    Examples:\n    * sort_array([]) => []\n    * sort_array([5]) => [5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5]) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n    * sort_array([2, 4, 3, 0, 1, 5, 6]) => [6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a copy of the array to avoid modifying the original\n    copied_array = array[:]\n\n    if len(copied_array) == 1:\n        return copied_array\n\n    # Determine sort order based on the sum of the first and last elements\n    first_element = copied_array[0]\n    last_element = copied_array[-1]\n    sum_first_last = first_element + last_element\n\n    if sum_first_last % 2 != 0:  # Odd sum -> ascending order\n        copied_array.sort()\n    else:  # Even sum -> descending order\n        copied_array.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return copied_array\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "```python\ndef get_row(lst, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all occurrences of x in a nested list and returns their 0-indexed coordinates.\n    Coordinates are sorted primarily by row ascending, then by column descending.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_coordinates = []\n\n    for row_idx, row_list in enumerate(lst):\n        for col_idx, element in enumerate(row_list):\n            if element == x:\n                found_coordinates.append((row_idx, col_idx))\n\n    # Sort the coordinates: primary by row (ascending), secondary by column (descending)\n    found_coordinates.sort(key=lambda coord: (coord[0], -coord[1]))\n\n    return found_coordinates\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\ndef encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Encrypts a string using a rotational cipher, shifting alphabetic characters by 4 positions.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged, and casing is preserved with wrap-around.\n    \"\"\"\n    SHIFT_VALUE = 4\n    ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n\n    encrypted_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            base = ord('a')\n            char_offset = ord(char) - base\n            shifted_offset = (char_offset + SHIFT_VALUE) % ALPHABET_SIZE\n            encrypted_chars.append(chr(base + shifted_offset))\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            base = ord('A')\n            char_offset = ord(char) - base\n            shifted_offset = (char_offset + SHIFT_VALUE) % ALPHABET_SIZE\n            encrypted_chars.append(chr(base + shifted_offset))\n        else:\n            encrypted_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)\n```"}
