{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "import math\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Returns the closest integer to a numerical string input.\n    Equidistant numbers (X.5) are rounded away from zero.\n    '''\n    num = float(value)\n\n    if num == int(num):\n        return int(num)\n\n    floor_num = math.floor(num)\n    ceil_num = math.ceil(num)\n\n    diff_floor = abs(num - floor_num)\n    diff_ceil = abs(num - ceil_num)\n\n    if diff_floor == diff_ceil:  # Equidistant case (e.g., X.5)\n        if num > 0:\n            return ceil_num  # Round up for positive numbers (away from zero)\n        else:\n            return floor_num # Round down for negative numbers (away from zero)\n    elif diff_floor < diff_ceil:\n        return floor_num\n    else:\n        return ceil_num"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all prime numbers strictly less than n.\n    This function adheres to specific constraints regarding input validation and helper functions.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function for primality test, defined inline as per requirements.\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a number is prime using trial division up to its square root.\n        Optimized for odd numbers after checking for 2.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        # Only check odd divisors up to the square root of num.\n        for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(num)) + 1, 2):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    # Main logic for count_up_to.\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    primes = [2] # Start with 2, the only even prime.\n\n    # Check odd numbers from 3 up to n-1.\n    for num in range(3, n, 2):\n        if is_prime(num):\n            primes.append(num)\n\n    return primes\n```"}
