{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Create a function that takes a value (string) representing a number\n    and returns the closest integer to it. If the number is equidistant\n    from two integers, round it away from zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    num = float(value)\n\n    # Calculate the floor and ceiling integers for the number.\n    floor_val = int(num // 1)\n    ceil_val = int(-(-num // 1))\n\n    # Calculate distances to the floor and ceiling values.\n    dist_to_floor = abs(num - floor_val)\n    dist_to_ceil = abs(num - ceil_val)\n\n    # Apply rounding rules: closest, with X.5 rounding away from zero.\n    if dist_to_floor < dist_to_ceil:\n        return floor_val\n    elif dist_to_ceil < dist_to_floor:\n        return ceil_val\n    else:  # Equidistant (e.g., X.5), round away from zero.\n        if num >= 0:\n            return ceil_val\n        else:\n            return floor_val\n\n```"}
